Yaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaay!


Whew.


This game took me awhile.  I played it for awhile, then I stopped for a
week, then I started again and so on.  So I don't remember all the
details but I'll try.

I started out ok.  I threw daggers like crazy and got Daggers to Expert
pretty fast while let my cat do most of the work.  I found a randomly
generated CoMR in a general store in the main dungeons.  Weird, that's
the third game in a row that that has happened.

I cleared out minetown and the mines, got like 4 luckstones.  Sobokan
had an AoR and I was still using the sack I started with with nary a
BoH in sight.

There was no Ludios this game, I checked every level with detect
treasure to be sure.

I found the quest level to be ... interesting.  The stairs at the
bottom (in the Master Assasins room) were on the left side and there
was apparently no way for me to get to the Nemesis.  I ended up going
one level up and level porting down.  I landed right next to the
Nemesis and got the MKoT and the BoO.  I also had to level port out.
Is that a bug?

Did Medusa's level and found another regular level below her.  It was
my last hope for the Fort but no luck.

At the castle I got an 0:3 WoW and wished up a B?oC (wished for 2, got
one), a BoH, B+oID, then a potion of unholy water so I could proof my
armor, more charging scrolls and two more magic markers.

Before I went to Hell I proofed everything and got my AC to -29.  I
wielded a silver saber through most of hell.

I tried to find a SDSM so I could wear my AoLS but none turned up
though one silver dragon I encountered I turned undead something like
10 times.  Is there no chance to get scales if the dragon doesn't drop
them the first time?

The end run with easy because of the plentiful cockatrice corpses.  I
had one in the Sanctum, on Water and Astral.  Then on Astral I got two
more :D.

I actually had 360 hp going into astral but I lost 66 hp to Death's
deadly touch because I was levitating so I couldn't jump away or throw
daggers at him.  I was afraid I would fall in a pit somehow and turn to
stone.

I stoned like 4 hero npcs this run but I didn't bother to break the
statues and grab whatever artifacts they had, which I usually do for
points, plus the wizard had a wand of death.

I managed to stone Maud the Lama right on the chaotic altar but she was
too heavy to lift so I didn't bring her with me. :D

Joeb, chaotic female orcish Rogue




